{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot7VoxelGIC","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VoxelGI"}],"title":"VoxelGI","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"VoxelGI","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Class","symbolKind":"class","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/cameraAttributes","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/data","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/size","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/subdiv-swift.property"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/bake(fromNode:createVisualDebug:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/debugBake()"]},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/godotClassName"]},{"title":"Enumerations","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/Subdiv-swift.enum"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Real-time global illumination (GI) probe.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VoxelGI","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI"},{"type":"text","text":"s are used to provide high-quality real-time indirect light and reflections to scenes. They precompute the effect of objects that emit light and the effect of static geometry to simulate the behavior of complex light in real-time. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI"},{"type":"text","text":"s need to be baked before having a visible effect. However, once baked, dynamic objects will receive light from them. Furthermore, lights can be fully dynamic or baked."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is only supported in the Forward+ rendering method, not Mobile or Compatibility."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Procedural generation:"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" can be baked in an exported project, which makes it suitable for procedurally generated or user-built levels as long as all the geometry is generated in advance. For games where geometry is generated at any time during gameplay, SDFGI is more suitable (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment\/sdfgiEnabled","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Performance:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is relatively demanding on the GPU and is not suited to low-end hardware such as integrated graphics (consider "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead). To improve performance, adjust "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/globalIllumination\/voxelGi\/quality"},{"type":"text","text":" and enable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/globalIllumination\/gi\/useHalfResolution"},{"type":"text","text":" in the Project Settings. To provide a fallback for low-end hardware, consider adding an option to disable "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in your project’s options menus. A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" node can be disabled by hiding it."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Meshes should have sufficiently thick walls to avoid light leaks (avoid one-sided walls). For interior levels, enclose your level geometry in a sufficiently large box and bridge the loops to close the mesh. To further prevent light leaks, you can also strategically place temporary ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MeshInstance3D","type":"reference"},{"text":" nodes with their ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/giMode-swift.property","type":"reference"},{"text":" set to ","type":"text"},{"code":"GeometryInstance3D\/GIMode\/`static```. These temporary nodes can then be hidden after baking the ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"VoxelGI`` node.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/voxelgi"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VisualInstance3D"]},{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/17SwiftGodotRuntime18VariantConvertibleP"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VisualInstance3D":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"VisualInstance3D","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"VisualInstance3D","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/visualinstance3d","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VisualInstance3D","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VisualInstance3D","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Parent of all visual 3D nodes."}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/MeshInstance3D":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/meshinstance3d","abstract":[{"text":"Node that instances meshes into a scenario.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MeshInstance3D","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MeshInstance3D","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MeshInstance3D","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MeshInstance3D"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/GeometryInstance3D/giMode-swift.property":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The global illumination mode to use for the whole geometry. To avoid inconsistent results, use a mode that matches the purpose of the mesh during gameplay (static\/dynamic)."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"giMode","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GeometryInstance3D","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot18GeometryInstance3DC","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"GIMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot18GeometryInstance3DC6GIModeO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/geometryinstance3d\/gimode-swift.property","kind":"symbol","title":"giMode","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/giMode-swift.property"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CameraAttributes":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/cameraattributes","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CameraAttributes"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Parent class for camera settings."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CameraAttributes"}],"title":"CameraAttributes","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CameraAttributes"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VoxelGI":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VoxelGI"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VoxelGI"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Real-time global illumination (GI) probe.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/voxelgi","title":"VoxelGI"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VoxelGIData":{"abstract":[{"text":"Contains baked voxel global illumination data for use in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI"},{"text":" node.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VoxelGIData","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGIData","role":"symbol","title":"VoxelGIData","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"VoxelGIData","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/voxelgidata","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VoxelGI/debugBake()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/voxelgi\/debugbake()","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/debugBake()","role":"symbol","title":"debugBake()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/bake(fromNode:createVisualDebug:)"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"create_visual_debug","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" enabled."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"debugBake","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VoxelGI/godotClassName":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/godotClassName","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"godotClassName","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StringName","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime10StringNameC"}],"type":"topic","title":"godotClassName","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/voxelgi\/godotclassname"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VoxelGI/subdiv-swift.property":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"subdiv","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VoxelGI","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot7VoxelGIC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Subdiv","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot7VoxelGIC6SubdivO"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/voxelgi\/subdiv-swift.property","abstract":[{"text":"Number of times to subdivide the grid that the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" operates on. A higher number results in finer detail and thus higher visual quality, while lower numbers result in better performance.","type":"text"}],"title":"subdiv","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/subdiv-swift.property"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Environment/sdfgiEnabled":{"title":"sdfgiEnabled","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"If ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":", enables signed distance field global illumination for meshes that have their ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/giMode-swift.property","isActive":true},{"text":" set to ``GeometryInstance3D\/GIMode\/`static```. SDFGI is a real-time global illumination technique that works well with procedurally generated and user-built levels, including in situations where geometry is created during gameplay. The signed distance field is automatically generated around the camera as it moves. Dynamic lights are supported, but dynamic occluders and emissive surfaces are not.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sdfgiEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/environment\/sdfgienabled","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment\/sdfgiEnabled"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VoxelGI/cameraAttributes":{"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CameraAttributes","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" resource that specifies exposure levels to bake at. Auto-exposure and non exposure properties will be ignored. Exposure settings should be used to reduce the dynamic range present when baking. If exposure is too high, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" will have banding artifacts or may have over-exposure artifacts.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cameraAttributes","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot16CameraAttributesC","text":"CameraAttributes","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI\/cameraAttributes","title":"cameraAttributes","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/voxelgi\/cameraattributes"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/LightmapGI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGI","role":"symbol","title":"LightmapGI","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LightmapGI"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LightmapGI"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Computes and stores baked lightmaps for fast global illumination.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/lightmapgi","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/SQ":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VoxelGI/bake(fromNode:createVisualDebug:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","k